      "title": "Bulb Toggle Ranges",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "n,k=map(int,input().split())\na=[0]*n\nfor _ in range(k):\n    l,r=map(int,input().split())\n    for i in range(l-1,r): a[i]^=1\nprint(' '.join(map(str,a)))",
      "statement": "A row of [[n]] bulbs is initially off ({{0}}).\nEach of the [[k]] operations flips every bulb in an inclusive range of positions, from [[l]] to [[r]]: an off bulb turns on and an on bulb turns off.\nPositions are 1-based, and operations are applied in the order given.\nPrint the final state of every bulb, from position 1 to position [[n]], as space-separated {{0}} and {{1}} values.",
